# Copy to .env.local for local development, or set these in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables (then redeploy).
#
# None of these are required. With no key the engine runs exactly as it does
# offline: the deterministic theme is a complete product, and the AI
# refinement pass simply never fires.
#
# NEVER prefix any of these with NEXT_PUBLIC_. That prefix inlines the value
# into the client bundle at build time, making it readable by every visitor —
# and once a key has shipped that way, rotating it is the only remedy.

# Server-side only. Read in app/api/read/route.ts.
# Create one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. If the photographs people
# capture are private, use a key from a project with billing enabled: Google
# may use free-tier inputs to improve its products.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to gemini-2.5-flash. Any Gemini model that accepts images
# and structured JSON output works, so moving to a newer Flash is a config
# change, not a code change.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
